                            <comment id="495244" author="behlendorf" created="Fri, 29 May 2026 16:50:36 +0000">&lt;p&gt;OpenZFS issue for this problem: &lt;a href="https://github.com/openzfs/zfs/issues/18402" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://github.com/openzfs/zfs/issues/18402&lt;/a&gt; &lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="494881" author="behlendorf" created="Fri, 22 May 2026 00:54:06 +0000">&lt;p&gt;A quick thing to try is setting the zfs module option `zfs_dmu_offset_next_sync` to `1`.  As long as Lustre isn't repeatedly dirtying the dnode from another thread holes should be reported reliably.  Quickly reporting holes when a dnode is dirty hasn't been implemented, but it would be nice!  One other thing to keep in mind is holes will reported at a recordsize granularity (not 4K).&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="494879" author="JIRAUSER19234" created="Thu, 21 May 2026 22:27:09 +0000">&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=behlendorf" class="user-hover" rel="behlendorf"&gt;behlendorf&lt;/a&gt; I was told you may be able to assist with this.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
